Subject: the display list says what it is drawing (the stereo class tags)

D-055, and the engine half of patch 0030's fold.

The visionOS stereo fold needs to know WHAT a projection is for, because the
three shapes PD hands the renderer need three different eye offsets. D-049
recovered that from the SHAPE of the matrix. On the simulator with N64 art that
read world 187440 / sky 1540 / gun 104 and looked right; on the user's headset
with the XBLA release on it read

    stereo_cls_world=2266415  stereo_cls_sky=2290014  stereo_cls_gun=247990

- a sky count equal to the world count. The shape of P is not a property of the
subject: PD's lists multiply into the projection (G_MTX_MUL with
G_MTX_PROJECTION) and 4J's mesh lists do it constantly, after which the product
is no longer axis-aligned and the shape test calls it sky. Half the geometry in
the room took the skew-only path, so half of it had no eye offset - two depths
for one scene, which is what the user reported three separate ways (bodies
floating above the floor, doors looking wrong, ramps "trippy, depth off").

So the engine says it instead, and this patch is that: a TAGGED G_NOOP naming
the class of the NEXT projection load. G_NOOP (0xc0) is already accepted and
ignored by gfx_pc (:3555) and by the N64 RSP, and neither reads w1, so a tag
costs one display-list command and changes no draw, tri, vert or texture
counter anywhere - which is why the oracle's gfx stream is unaffected.
gDPSetBlendMask is aliased to an UNtagged gDPNoOp, so the payload carries a
magic in its high half and w1 == 0 stays "not ours".

Only four sites in the whole tree carry a tag, because an untagged projection
load is WORLD and a MUL into the projection keeps the class of the load:

  * vi.c vi0000ab78()          - SKY. The camera's rotation is folded into P
                                 and the modelview is identity.
  * vi.c vi0000aca4()          - GUN when it was called with the viewmodel's
    vi.c viSetPerspectiveWithFov()  znear of 1.5 (bondgun.c:11426/11441),
                                 WORLD at menuRenderModel's 10. The znear is a
                                 plain argument here, so this is the engine's
                                 own number rather than one read back out of a
                                 matrix.
  * menu.c menuRender()        - a FLAT SPAN, because Q-026 is answered
                                 "flatten" and PD's dialogs are not the
                                 matrix-free NDC rectangles §2.4 assumed: most
                                 of the chrome is projected geometry through
                                 func0f0d479c's own frustum, menuRenderModel
                                 installs a perspective of its own, the
                                 hudpiece uses the world's and the health bar
                                 is drawn in the world projection inside the
                                 span. Five projections, one dialog - so the
                                 span is what reaches all five.

The emission is under #ifndef PLATFORM_N64 so a matching N64 build is
byte-identical.

diff --git a/src/game/menu.c b/src/game/menu.c
index e71abb17e..604829745 100644
--- a/src/game/menu.c
+++ b/src/game/menu.c
@@ -6083,6 +6083,23 @@ Gfx *menuRender(Gfx *gdl)
 
 	gdl = func0f0d479c(gdl);
 
+#ifndef PLATFORM_N64
+	// FLAT SPAN (D-055, Q-026 answered "flatten"): everything menuRender draws
+	// is identical in both eyes and sits exactly ON the panel.
+	//
+	// PD's menus are NOT the matrix-free NDC rectangles the 3D plan assumed.
+	// func0f0d479c() above installs a real frustum (guFrustumF, znear 10,
+	// savebuffer.c:70) with a depth-FLATTENED viewport, most of the chrome is
+	// projected geometry through it (ten gSPVertex sites in menugfx.c alone),
+	// menuRenderModel() installs a perspective of its own for the rotating
+	// model, the hudpiece uses the world's, and the health bar is drawn in the
+	// world projection inside this very span. Five projections, one dialog — so
+	// this is a SPAN and not a projection class, and it is the span that reaches
+	// all five. The user, in the headset on 0.0.0.9: "pause menu has depth
+	// intersecting the world".
+	gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLSPAN_FLAT_BEGIN);
+#endif
+
 	gSPDisplayList(gdl++, var800613a0);
 
 	// Render the background
@@ -6445,6 +6462,9 @@ Gfx *menuRender(Gfx *gdl)
 
 #ifndef PLATFORM_N64
 	gSPClearExtraGeometryModeEXT(gdl++, G_ASPECT_MODE_EXT);
+	// ...and the flat span closes (D-055), before the world projection comes
+	// back at func0f0d49c8() so that nothing after it is flattened.
+	gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLSPAN_FLAT_END);
 #endif
 
 	gdl = func0f0d49c8(gdl);
diff --git a/src/include/gbiex.h b/src/include/gbiex.h
index fb7591e30..6eb88ea3d 100644
--- a/src/include/gbiex.h
+++ b/src/include/gbiex.h
@@ -212,6 +212,53 @@
 #define G_SETTILEOFFSET_EXT          0x4d
 #define G_MESH_EXT                   0x4e
 
+/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
+/* DISPLAY-LIST CLASS TAGS (visionOS 3D stereo mode, D-055).                */
+/*                                                                          */
+/* The stereo fold in port/fast3d/gfx_pc.cpp needs to know WHAT the list is  */
+/* drawing, because the three shapes of projection PD hands the renderer     */
+/* need three different eye offsets. It used to RECOVER that from the shape  */
+/* of the projection matrix, and that guess broke on 4J's XBLA art: the      */
+/* device counters came back world 2.27M / sky 2.29M / gun 248k, a sky count */
+/* equal to the world count, and half the geometry got the wrong offset —    */
+/* which is what the user saw in the headset as bodies floating above the      */
+/* floor and ramps reading "trippy, depth off".                             */
+/*                                                                          */
+/* So the engine says it instead. These are TAGGED G_NOOPs (gbi.h:3826):     */
+/* opcode 0xc0 is already accepted and ignored by gfx_pc (:3555) and by the  */
+/* N64 RSP, and w1 is never read by either, so a tag costs one command and   */
+/* changes no draw, tri, vert or texture count anywhere. `gDPSetBlendMask`   */
+/* is aliased to an UNtagged gDPNoOp (gbi.h:2351), whose w1 is 0, so the     */
+/* payload carries a magic in its high half and w1 == 0 is "not ours".       */
+/*                                                                          */
+/* A tag applies to the NEXT projection LOAD and one only — the pending-tag  */
+/* shape gfx_pc already uses for G_SETFONTGLYPH_EXT. An untagged load is     */
+/* PD_DLCLASS_WORLD, which is why only the sky's and the gun's own two       */
+/* projection sites carry one and the other thirty-odd loads in this engine  */
+/* need no change at all. A G_MTX_MUL into the projection KEEPS the class,   */
+/* which is the half the shape test could not do.                           */
+/*                                                                          */
+/* MENU is not a projection class but a span: menuRender() flattens whatever */
+/* it draws (Q-026, answered "flatten"), through all five of its own         */
+/* projection paths, so it brackets itself instead.                         */
+/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------ */
+
+#define PD_DLTAG_MAGIC          0x5044u   /* 'PD'; 0 is an untagged noop */
+#define PD_DLTAG(x)             (((unsigned int)PD_DLTAG_MAGIC << 16) | ((x) & 0xffffu))
+#define PD_DLTAG_PAYLOAD(w1)    ((unsigned int)(w1) & 0xffffu)
+#define PD_DLTAG_IS_OURS(w1)    ((((unsigned int)(w1)) >> 16) == (unsigned int)PD_DLTAG_MAGIC)
+
+/* Projection classes, one-shot: they name the next projection load. */
+#define PD_DLCLASS_WORLD   0   /* the full eye offset and convergence */
+#define PD_DLCLASS_SKY     1   /* convergence skew only: a camera-basis fold */
+#define PD_DLCLASS_GUN     2   /* the viewmodel, converged at its own depth */
+#define PD_DLCLASS_FLAT    3   /* no fold: identical in both eyes, on the panel */
+/* Span markers, sticky between the two: flatten everything drawn inside. */
+#define PD_DLSPAN_FLAT_BEGIN  8
+#define PD_DLSPAN_FLAT_END    9
+
+#define gDPPdDlTag(pkt, x) gDPNoOpTag(pkt, PD_DLTAG(x))
+
 /* G_EXTRAGEOMETRYMODE flags */
 
 #define G_INVERT_CULLING_EXT     0x00000001
diff --git a/src/lib/vi.c b/src/lib/vi.c
index 78e21170d..2226dcc17 100644
--- a/src/lib/vi.c
+++ b/src/lib/vi.c
@@ -549,6 +549,14 @@ Gfx *vi0000ab78(Gfx *gdl)
 	sp48 = gfxAllocateMatrix();
 	guMtxF2L(sp50.m, sp48);
 
+#ifndef PLATFORM_N64
+	// SKY (D-055): the camera's ROTATION is folded into the projection above and
+	// the modelview is identity, so a view-space translation folded into this
+	// matrix would be a WORLD-space shift. The sky also draws at 2 x zfar, where
+	// the correct disparity is exactly the convergence skew's infinity term. The
+	// stereo fold reads the tag and applies the skew only.
+	gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, PD_DLCLASS_SKY);
+#endif
 	gSPMatrix(gdl++, OS_K0_TO_PHYSICAL(sp4c), G_MTX_NOPUSH | G_MTX_LOAD | G_MTX_PROJECTION);
 	gSPMatrix(gdl++, OS_K0_TO_PHYSICAL(sp48), G_MTX_NOPUSH | G_MTX_LOAD | G_MTX_MODELVIEW);
 	gSPPerspNormalize(gdl++, sp46);
@@ -565,6 +573,14 @@ Gfx *vi0000aca4(Gfx *gdl, f32 znear, f32 zfar)
 	guPerspectiveF(tmp.m, &scale, g_ViBackData->fovy, g_ViBackData->aspect, znear, zfar, 1);
 	guMtxF2L(tmp.m, mtx);
 
+#ifndef PLATFORM_N64
+	// GUN (D-055). bgunRender() calls this with znear 1.5 for the viewmodel
+	// (bondgun.c:11426) against the world's own 30 (vi.c:41); menuRenderModel()
+	// calls it with 10 for the rotating character model. The znear is a plain
+	// argument here, so the class is decided from the ENGINE's own number rather
+	// than recovered from the matrix, which is the whole point of D-055.
+	gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, (znear < 5.0f) ? PD_DLCLASS_GUN : PD_DLCLASS_WORLD);
+#endif
 	gSPMatrix(gdl++, OS_K0_TO_PHYSICAL(mtx), G_MTX_NOPUSH | G_MTX_LOAD | G_MTX_PROJECTION);
 	gSPPerspNormalize(gdl++, scale);
 
@@ -586,6 +602,8 @@ Gfx *viSetPerspectiveWithFov(Gfx *gdl, f32 fovy, f32 znear, f32 zfar)
 	guPerspectiveF(tmp.m, &scale, fovy, g_ViBackData->aspect, znear, zfar, 1);
 	guMtxF2L(tmp.m, mtx);
 
+	// GUN (D-055): the COD-aim sights path, bondgun.c:11441, znear 1.5.
+	gDPPdDlTag(gdl++, (znear < 5.0f) ? PD_DLCLASS_GUN : PD_DLCLASS_WORLD);
 	gSPMatrix(gdl++, OS_K0_TO_PHYSICAL(mtx), G_MTX_NOPUSH | G_MTX_LOAD | G_MTX_PROJECTION);
 	gSPPerspNormalize(gdl++, scale);
 
